[E0216] Error: only a struct's or an enum's type parameter has a default
    ╭─[ err/290_default_type_arguments/main.wip:30:12 ]
    │
 30 │ fn generic<T = i64>(x: T): T = x
    │            ───┬───
    │               ╰───── a default
    │
    │ Note: a default says what a type is where it is written with fewer type arguments; a function's are inferred where it is called, and an `extend` block names every one
────╯
[E0338] Error: `extend` of `Pool` must name its type parameters
    ╭─[ err/290_default_type_arguments/main.wip:32:8 ]
    │
 32 │ extend Pool<T> {}
    │        ───┬──
    │           ╰──── `Pool` has 2 type parameters: `<T, K>`
    │
    │ Note 1: an `extend` block binds the type's parameters under the names it writes, one for each
    │
    │ Note 2: a default type argument is for a use of the type; the block names the parameter it stands for too
────╯
